    skos:definition "an artificial butter made with tallow, oil, and other ingredients, also known as margarine. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 448]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_animal_fats_tallow): Butterine is the trade name for oleomargarine (cf. htc:0976). Layer-1 observations: 8 rows, 1886–1886. Series: HCPP_Annual Statement of Trade ×8. Units: CWTS (Hundredweights) ×8. Top routes: Holland → United Kingdom ×1; World → United Kingdom ×1; Belgium → United Kingdom ×1; Russia → United Kingdom ×1."@en ;
